    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 299.04,
      "durationSeconds": 3.36,
      "text": "however because the hacker knows the"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 300.72,
      "durationSeconds": 3.12,
      "text": "hash came from a password"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 302.4,
      "durationSeconds": 2.96,
      "text": "they can use their knowledge of human"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 303.84,
      "durationSeconds": 2.24,
      "text": "nature to narrow down the possible"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 305.36,
      "durationSeconds": 2.8,
      "text": "guesses"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 306.08,
      "durationSeconds": 4,
      "text": "which makes guessing feasible"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 308.16,
      "durationSeconds": 4,
      "text": "furthermore they can use lists of the"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 310.08,
      "durationSeconds": 3.92,
      "text": "most common passwords to pre-generate a"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 312.16,
      "durationSeconds": 3.52,
      "text": "huge database of hashes"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 314,
      "durationSeconds": 3.6,
      "text": "so all they need to do is to compare"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 315.68,
      "durationSeconds": 3.04,
      "text": "their huge database to your database to"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 317.6,
      "durationSeconds": 2.879,
      "text": "find matches"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 318.72,
      "durationSeconds": 4.479,
      "text": "these databases are known as rainbow"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 320.479,
      "durationSeconds": 4.56,
      "text": "tables how can we defend against this"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 323.199,
      "durationSeconds": 3.601,
      "text": "let's go to b-tier for a technique that"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 325.039,
      "durationSeconds": 3.44,
      "text": "protects against rainbow tables but not"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 326.8,
      "durationSeconds": 4.32,
      "text": "against dictionary attacks"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 328.479,
      "durationSeconds": 3.761,
      "text": "it's a technique called salting when the"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 331.12,
      "durationSeconds": 2.72,
      "text": "user signs up"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 332.24,
      "durationSeconds": 3.44,
      "text": "rather than directly hashing each"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 333.84,
      "durationSeconds": 3.84,
      "text": "password we can first generate a short"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 335.68,
      "durationSeconds": 4.48,
      "text": "random string called the salt"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 337.68,
      "durationSeconds": 3.84,
      "text": "then we prepend it to the string before"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 340.16,
      "durationSeconds": 2.879,
      "text": "running the hash"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 341.52,
      "durationSeconds": 4.16,
      "text": "we then store the salt next to the"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 343.039,
      "durationSeconds": 4.401,
      "text": "hashed password when the user logs in we"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 345.68,
      "durationSeconds": 3.68,
      "text": "can prepend the remembered salt to the"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 347.44,
      "durationSeconds": 3.759,
      "text": "password they entered and hash to see if"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 349.36,
      "durationSeconds": 3.679,
      "text": "it matches the stored password"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 351.199,
      "durationSeconds": 3.681,
      "text": "it's important to use the same salt at"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 353.039,
      "durationSeconds": 3.361,
      "text": "login that was generated during signup"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 354.88,
      "durationSeconds": 2.4,
      "text": "which is why we want to store it in the"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 356.4,
      "durationSeconds": 2.56,
      "text": "database"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 357.28,
      "durationSeconds": 3.44,
      "text": "otherwise the user wouldn't be able to"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 358.96,
      "durationSeconds": 3.519,
      "text": "log in even with the right password"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 360.72,
      "durationSeconds": 3.52,
      "text": "because the hashes wouldn't match"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 362.479,
      "durationSeconds": 3.601,
      "text": "this makes rainbow tables useless"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 364.24,
      "durationSeconds": 4.88,
      "text": "because their databases only contain"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 366.08,
      "durationSeconds": 4.959,
      "text": "non-salted hashes for example these"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 369.12,
      "durationSeconds": 3.76,
      "text": "users have the password qwerty but the"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 371.039,
      "durationSeconds": 3.921,
      "text": "table doesn't match anymore"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 372.88,
      "durationSeconds": 4.24,
      "text": "this has the added benefit of decorating"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 374.96,
      "durationSeconds": 4.239,
      "text": "users who have the same password"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 377.12,
      "durationSeconds": 4.16,
      "text": "previously if two users use the same"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 379.199,
      "durationSeconds": 3.921,
      "text": "password their hashes would be the same"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 381.28,
      "durationSeconds": 3.6,
      "text": "which is not ideal because you can see"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 383.12,
      "durationSeconds": 2.88,
      "text": "that they have the same password even if"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 384.88,
      "durationSeconds": 2.48,
      "text": "you don't know what the password"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 386,
      "durationSeconds": 3.039,
      "text": "actually is"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 387.36,
      "durationSeconds": 3.44,
      "text": "now even though their passwords are the"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 389.039,
      "durationSeconds": 3.201,
      "text": "same their salts are different so the"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 390.8,
      "durationSeconds": 3.839,
      "text": "hashes are different"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 392.24,
      "durationSeconds": 4,
      "text": "but why is this still beat here remember"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 394.639,
      "durationSeconds": 3.201,
      "text": "the other issue we talked about which is"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 396.24,
      "durationSeconds": 3.12,
      "text": "dictionary attacks"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 397.84,
      "durationSeconds": 3.04,
      "text": "an attacker with a list of common"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 399.36,
      "durationSeconds": 3.52,
      "text": "passwords can still try all of them"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 400.88,
      "durationSeconds": 3.12,
      "text": "against the hash using the salt"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 402.88,
      "durationSeconds": 2.96,
      "text": "they don't get the benefit of"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 404,
      "durationSeconds": 2.88,
      "text": "precomputation but they can still start"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 405.84,
      "durationSeconds": 2.799,
      "text": "from scratch"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 406.88,
      "durationSeconds": 3.68,
      "text": "furthermore specialized hardware like"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 408.639,
      "durationSeconds": 2.4,
      "text": "gpus have made it possible for people to"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 410.56,
      "durationSeconds": 2.56,
      "text": "compute"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 411.039,
      "durationSeconds": 3.841,
      "text": "billions of hashes per second which"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 413.12,
      "durationSeconds": 2.72,
      "text": "translates into billions of guests per"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 414.88,
      "durationSeconds": 2.879,
      "text": "second"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 415.84,
      "durationSeconds": 4.079,
      "text": "how on earth do we stop this one let's"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 417.759,
      "durationSeconds": 4.401,
      "text": "see what a tier has to say"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 419.919,
      "durationSeconds": 3.601,
      "text": "an a tier is using a specialized"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 422.16,
      "durationSeconds": 3.12,
      "text": "password hashing function that is"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 423.52,
      "durationSeconds": 3.519,
      "text": "deliberately slow"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 425.28,
      "durationSeconds": 3.28,
      "text": "the previous hash functions we discussed"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 427.039,
      "durationSeconds": 3.201,
      "text": "are designed to be fast because they're"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 428.56,
      "durationSeconds": 2.88,
      "text": "used for other applications besides"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 430.24,
      "durationSeconds": 3.44,
      "text": "passwords"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 431.44,
      "durationSeconds": 4.56,
      "text": "password hashing functions like bcrypt"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 433.68,
      "durationSeconds": 2.88,
      "text": "script and argon 2 come with salting for"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 436,
      "durationSeconds": 2.479,
      "text": "free"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 436.56,
      "durationSeconds": 3.52,
      "text": "and more importantly are designed to be"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 438.479,
      "durationSeconds": 3.681,
      "text": "really really really slow"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 440.08,
      "durationSeconds": 3.36,
      "text": "to consume lots of power and to take"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 442.16,
      "durationSeconds": 3.039,
      "text": "lots of memory"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 443.44,
      "durationSeconds": 3.199,
      "text": "it sounds weird but this is actually on"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 445.199,
      "durationSeconds": 3.681,
      "text": "purpose to defend against the"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 446.639,
      "durationSeconds": 4.081,
      "text": "overwhelming power of hardware"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 448.88,
      "durationSeconds": 4,
      "text": "the billions of hashes per second we saw"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 450.72,
      "durationSeconds": 3.28,
      "text": "a moment ago can be slowed down to mere"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 452.88,
      "durationSeconds": 3.039,
      "text": "thousands per second"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 454,
      "durationSeconds": 3.68,
      "text": "if not even slower because you can"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 455.919,
      "durationSeconds": 2.481,
      "text": "actually choose the level of slowness"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 457.68,
      "durationSeconds": 3.12,
      "text": "you want"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 458.4,
      "durationSeconds": 4.32,
      "text": "this is known as the work factor with"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 460.8,
      "durationSeconds": 3.519,
      "text": "only thousands of guesses per second"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 462.72,
      "durationSeconds": 3.12,
      "text": "that's still enough to easily go through"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 464.319,
      "durationSeconds": 3.28,
      "text": "the most common passwords"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 465.84,
      "durationSeconds": 3.44,
      "text": "but it's not enough to break tougher or"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 467.599,
      "durationSeconds": 3.6,
      "text": "more obscure passwords"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 469.28,
      "durationSeconds": 3.28,
      "text": "with the high enough work factor hackers"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 471.199,
      "durationSeconds": 3.28,
      "text": "might be able to break some of the"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 472.56,
      "durationSeconds": 2.72,
      "text": "passwords in your system but not all of"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 474.479,
      "durationSeconds": 2.801,
      "text": "them"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 475.28,
      "durationSeconds": 4.319,
      "text": "after all the goal of security is not to"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 477.28,
      "durationSeconds": 4.16,
      "text": "be immune to attacks which is impossible"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 479.599,
      "durationSeconds": 4.241,
      "text": "but to hinder attackers enough that they"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 481.44,
      "durationSeconds": 4,
      "text": "turn their attention to other places"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 483.84,
      "durationSeconds": 3.28,
      "text": "as a concrete example let's look at"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 485.44,
      "durationSeconds": 3.84,
      "text": "bcrypt the output of b"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 487.12,
      "durationSeconds": 3.6,
      "text": "crypt looks like this it has a prefix"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 489.28,
      "durationSeconds": 2.72,
      "text": "that identifies the output as a"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 490.72,
      "durationSeconds": 4.08,
      "text": "decrypted thing"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 492,
      "durationSeconds": 4.8,
      "text": "a work factor a 22 character salt and a"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 494.8,
      "durationSeconds": 3.76,
      "text": "31 character hash"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 496.8,
      "durationSeconds": 3.92,
      "text": "the most interesting thing about this is"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 498.56,
      "durationSeconds": 4.24,
      "text": "that the work factor is exponential"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 500.72,
      "durationSeconds": 4.56,
      "text": "when you increase the work factor by 1"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 502.8,
      "durationSeconds": 4.399,
      "text": "the function becomes twice as slow"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 505.28,
      "durationSeconds": 3.599,
      "text": "here's a graph of decrypt hash time by"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 507.199,
      "durationSeconds": 4.161,
      "text": "work factor on my laptop"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 508.879,
      "durationSeconds": 3.84,
      "text": "the exponential increase is quite clear"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 511.36,
      "durationSeconds": 3.52,
      "text": "most folks recommend setting it to"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 512.719,
      "durationSeconds": 4.161,
      "text": "around 15 for real use cases which takes"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 514.88,
      "durationSeconds": 3.92,
      "text": "1.3 seconds on my laptop"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 516.88,
      "durationSeconds": 3.519,
      "text": "fun fact when it was first published the"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 518.8,
      "durationSeconds": 3.28,
      "text": "recommended work factor was just"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 520.399,
      "durationSeconds": 4.321,
      "text": "six which would take just two"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 522.08,
      "durationSeconds": 5.6,
      "text": "milliseconds on my modern laptop"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 524.72,
      "durationSeconds": 4.239,
      "text": "so is that it are we done is there an"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 527.68,
      "durationSeconds": 3.92,
      "text": "even higher tier"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 528.959,
      "durationSeconds": 3.681,
      "text": "s tier it's kind of a trick answer but"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 531.6,
      "durationSeconds": 3.919,
      "text": "there is"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 532.64,
      "durationSeconds": 4.319,
      "text": "s tier is not storing passwords at all"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 535.519,
      "durationSeconds": 2.801,
      "text": "as we've learned in this video storing"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 536.959,
      "durationSeconds": 3.521,
      "text": "passwords is quite tricky"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 538.32,
      "durationSeconds": 3.36,
      "text": "so consider ways to avoid doing it at"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 540.48,
      "durationSeconds": 2.64,
      "text": "all for example"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 541.68,
      "durationSeconds": 3.36,
      "text": "you can use other authentication"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 543.12,
      "durationSeconds": 3.76,
      "text": "services like sign in with google or"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 545.04,
      "durationSeconds": 3.6,
      "text": "sign in with facebook and others"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 546.88,
      "durationSeconds": 3.44,
      "text": "so that users can log into your product"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 548.64,
      "durationSeconds": 2.639,
      "text": "using an established authentication"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 550.32,
      "durationSeconds": 3.04,
      "text": "platform"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 551.279,
      "durationSeconds": 3.601,
      "text": "not only is it more convenient for users"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 553.36,
      "durationSeconds": 2.32,
      "text": "you get to sleep better at night knowing"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 554.88,
      "durationSeconds": 2.8,
      "text": "that your system"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 555.68,
      "durationSeconds": 3.44,
      "text": "doesn't have any passwords at all in it"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 557.68,
      "durationSeconds": 3.76,
      "text": "that's all i have for today"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 559.12,
      "durationSeconds": 3.839,
      "text": "let's recap first we looked at storing"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 561.44,
      "durationSeconds": 3.68,
      "text": "passwords in plain text which means"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 562.959,
      "durationSeconds": 4.161,
      "text": "anyone can easily access them"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 565.12,
      "durationSeconds": 3.76,
      "text": "so we considered encrypting them which"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 567.12,
      "durationSeconds": 3.2,
      "text": "is not ideal because their original form"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 568.88,
      "durationSeconds": 2.959,
      "text": "can still be recovered"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 570.32,
      "durationSeconds": 3.44,
      "text": "we introduced hashing to make that"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 571.839,
      "durationSeconds": 3.761,
      "text": "impossible but we saw that people can"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 573.76,
      "durationSeconds": 3.519,
      "text": "pre-compute huge rainbow tables to"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 575.6,
      "durationSeconds": 3.84,
      "text": "quickly break passwords"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 577.279,
      "durationSeconds": 4.081,
      "text": "to counteract that we introduce salting"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 579.44,
      "durationSeconds": 3.519,
      "text": "which individualizes each password with"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 581.36,
      "durationSeconds": 3.52,
      "text": "a random string called the salt"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 582.959,
      "durationSeconds": 4.241,
      "text": "so that precomputed databases don't work"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 584.88,
      "durationSeconds": 3.76,
      "text": "anymore unfortunately hardware is so"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 587.2,
      "durationSeconds": 3.199,
      "text": "fast that even without precomputed"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 588.64,
      "durationSeconds": 3.68,
      "text": "databases attackers can still try"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 590.399,
      "durationSeconds": 3.521,
      "text": "billions of guesses per second"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 592.32,
      "durationSeconds": 3.28,
      "text": "so we need to switch to deliberately"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 593.92,
      "durationSeconds": 4.08,
      "text": "slow password hashing functions that"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 595.6,
      "durationSeconds": 4.4,
      "text": "greatly decrease the rate of guesses"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 598,
      "durationSeconds": 3.76,
      "text": "finally we bypass the whole problem by"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 600,
      "durationSeconds": 2.56,
      "text": "considering how to not store passwords"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 601.76,
      "durationSeconds": 2.8,
      "text": "at all"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 602.56,
      "durationSeconds": 3.76,
      "text": "i hope this was helpful if you enjoyed"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 604.56,
      "durationSeconds": 3.44,
      "text": "this video please consider sharing it"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 606.32,
      "durationSeconds": 2.24,
      "text": "with somebody else who might also enjoy"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 608,
      "durationSeconds": 9.839,
      "text": "it"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 608.56,
